"""Ready-made choice stories (Persian): complete, hand-written branching stories with ORIGINAL characters, so the owner can start from a real story even when no
text model is reachable (the planner falls back to these instead of placeholder text), and a language model has real examples of the form.

Every story is plain data: a cast of stick-figure specs (see render/stick/spec.py) and posts (id, title, text, location = a stick background, characters, pose,
expression, choices, ending). `tests/test_story_templates.py` runs each one through graph.validate: forward numbering, no dead ends, every post reachable, a good
ending, labels and texts inside the limits. Nothing here is copied from any existing story, game or channel; the prison-escape plot is the owner's own idea
(one prisoner, one night, a few decisions) written from scratch.

The brand story (`chagher_coach`) uses only facts published on the product's own site (see docs/CHOICE_STORIES.md): a draft in under a minute, sign-up in under a
minute with a free start and no credit card, the coach's own standing instruction, a branded PDF, and "the final decision is the coach's". It promises no result and
invents no customer, price or statistic.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import copy


def P(pid: str, title: str, text: str, where: str, who: list[str], pose: str = "stand", expr: str = "neutral", go: tuple = (), end: str = "") -> dict:
    return {"id": pid, "title": title, "text": text, "location": where, "characters": list(who), "pose": pose, "expression": expr,
            "choices": [{"label": a, "to": b} for a, b in go], "ending": end, "kind": "ending" if end else "story"}


def C(name: str, role: str, appearance: str, **spec) -> dict:
    return {"name": name, "role": role, "appearance": appearance, "spec": spec}


